WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:04.395
A planning screen can produce a manifest or readiness report without deploying

00:00:04.395 --> 00:00:08.611
anything. In the retained Foundation planning tools, inspect the returned

00:00:08.917 --> 00:00:11.720
read-only and execution-enabled flags.

00:00:11.807 --> 00:00:16.244
A count of passed checks is not a count of imaged nodes or proof of a completed

00:00:16.244 --> 00:00:20.866
cluster. For Cluster A, inspect the node serials, addresses,

00:00:20.895 --> 00:00:24.139
image selections and credential references in the plan.

00:00:24.328 --> 00:00:27.370
Review each blocker and unsupported operation.

00:00:27.613 --> 00:00:32.128
Do not infer discovered hardware, an approved maintenance window or live

00:00:32.136 --> 00:00:34.282
authorization from a generated file.

00:00:34.631 --> 00:00:38.975
When using classic Foundation VM, open its supported deployment workflow

00:00:39.026 --> 00:00:42.602
and review its own validation, approval and mutation gates.

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:45.042
Foundation remains the imaging service.

00:00:45.313 --> 00:00:49.572
The separate retired Native pipeline option does not become available because
another

00:00:49.580 --> 00:00:51.321
feature uses the word native.

00:00:51.799 --> 00:00:56.321
A connectivity or credential probe establishes only the checks it performed from its

00:00:56.321 --> 00:01:00.526
stated source. It does not prove later reboot behavior, VLAN

00:01:00.526 --> 00:01:02.972
reachability or end-to-end imaging.

00:01:03.214 --> 00:01:07.558
Validate the selected hardware and software combination in an approved
environment

00:01:07.609 --> 00:01:09.740
before enabling guarded live changes.

00:01:10.142 --> 00:01:14.699
Retain the plan, approval, actual job output and target verification

00:01:14.792 --> 00:01:19.392
separately. Use actual Foundation telemetry during deployment and reconcile

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.835
uncertain submissions before a new attempt.

00:01:22.066 --> 00:01:26.674
This lesson demonstrates those boundaries with simulated data and performs no

00:01:26.674 --> 00:01:27.434
imaging.
